    {
      "question": "1. Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "The current reading was received and sent to the landlord (event 013). The landlord has set the next reading for 15 September 2025 (event 015). Nothing is outstanding until 1 September 2025, when the next photo should be requested from the tenant. The ongoing recurrence after September is not yet confirmed."
    },
    {
      "question": "2. What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email the landlord Ava to confirm the 15 September date (done, MSG-102). SMS the tenant Miles Fletcher to thank him and say the next reading is due 15 September (done, MSG-103). Follow-up FUP-101 on 2025-09-01 asks the tenant for the September photo by email. The job is on hold until then."
    },
    {
      "question": "3. Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "No. The landlord has given a clear instruction, the photo has been received, and the action is routine. The only open point (the recurrence after September) can be confirmed with the landlord when the September cycle starts, so no escalation is needed."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A5",
      "description": "Put NBL-010-recurring on hold until 2025-09-01 (read back verified after the first attempt used the wrong ticket ref)."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Scheduled follow-up FUP-101 for 2025-09-01 to request the September solar photo from the tenant."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Emailed landlord Ava confirming the 15 September 2025 reading date (MSG-102)."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "SMSed tenant Miles Fletcher that the photo was received and the next reading is due 15 September (MSG-103)."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "handling": "put_on_hold failed because I used the case id '010-recurring' instead of the real ticket ref. I listed tickets, found NBL-010-recurring, and re-applied the hold, which verified as A5."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "The original request and the ticket say 'every 3 months' with the next reading due mid-June. The landlord's latest message (event 015, 2025-01-17) says the next reading is 15 September. I trusted the landlord's latest instruction.",
    "Event 008 says the call came from 'Oakfield Compliance', but the job is logged under Northbridge Lettings. Not material to this task, but noted.",
    "The tenant's reply (event 012) has no email address, so the tenant was messaged by SMS on the phone number from his own signature. The landlord email uses the existing thread (event 015)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The landlord's 15 September date is the correct next due date for the reading.",
    "The tenant's phone number in event 012 is accurate and can be used for SMS."
  ]
}

